====== Leetcode 88. Merge Sorted Array (28th Feb)=======
Step-by-step algorithm for merging two sorted arrays:

Step 1: Initialize a pointer k at the last index of nums1 (m + n - 1).
This is where the largest element will be placed.

Step 2: Move m to the last valid element of nums1 (m - 1).

Step 3: Move n to the last element of nums2 (n - 1).

Step 4: Compare elements from the end of both arrays while both pointers are valid (m >= 0 and n >= 0).

Sub-step 4a: If nums1[m] is greater than nums2[n],
place nums1[m] at index k,
then decrease m.

Sub-step 4b: Otherwise,
place nums2[n] at index k,
then decrease n.

Sub-step 4c: Decrease k after placing each element.

Step 5: After the loop, check if any elements are left in nums2 (n >= 0).

Sub-step 5a: If yes, copy all remaining elements of nums2 into nums1 from index k backwards.

Step 6: No need to check remaining elements of nums1 because they are already in correct position.

Step 7: After completion, nums1 contains all elements from both arrays in sorted order.

Time Complexity:
You traverse each element at most once.
Time Complexity = O(m + n)

Space Complexity:
No extra array is used.
Space Complexity = O(1)



          --------------> Code <---------------
class Solution {
    public void merge(int[] nums1, int m, int[] nums2, int n) {
        int k=m+n-1;
        m=m-1;
        n=n-1;
        
        while(m>=0 && n>=0){
            if(nums1[m]>nums2[n]){
                nums1[k]=nums1[m--];
            }else{
                nums1[k]=nums2[n--];
            }
            k--;
        }
        while(n>=0){
            nums1[k--]=nums2[n--];
        }

    }
}
